{"bendscript":"0.1","blocks":[{"id":"blk-70218","kind":"heading","level":1,"spans":[{"id":"spn-102968","text":"κ Integration Spec: Product-Level Specification"}]},{"id":"blk-70219","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-102969","text":"Version 0.2.0 — Normalized"}]},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-70221","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-102970","text":"How the cyclicity invariant κ is computed, surfaced, and used across Graphonomous, BendScript, Deliberatic, TickTickClock, and the [&] Protocol.  "},{"id":"spn-102971","marks":["bold"],"text":"v0.2.0 changes (from Codex review):"},{"id":"spn-102972","text":" - Normalized all field names to a single canonical schema (§2.4) - Resolved tool naming: "},{"id":"spn-102973","marks":["code"],"text":"analyze_topology"},{"id":"spn-102974","text":" is the standalone tool; "},{"id":"spn-102975","marks":["code"],"text":"retrieve_context"},{"id":"spn-102976","text":" gains a "},{"id":"spn-102977","marks":["code"],"text":"topology"},{"id":"spn-102978","text":" field — no "},{"id":"spn-102979","marks":["code"],"text":"memory_recall_with_topology"},{"id":"spn-102980","text":" tool - Fixed approximation representation: "},{"id":"spn-102981","marks":["code"],"text":"kappa"},{"id":"spn-102982","text":" is always an integer; large SCCs add "},{"id":"spn-102983","marks":["code"],"text":"approximate: true"},{"id":"spn-102984","text":" (no "},{"id":"spn-102985","marks":["code"],"text":"exact"},{"id":"spn-102986","text":" field) - Added instrumentation requirements (§7) - Clarified BendScript directed-edge policy (§4.3)"}]}],"id":"blk-70220","kind":"quote"},{"id":"blk-70222","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-102987","text":"1. Overview"}]},{"id":"blk-70223","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-102988","text":"κ (kappa) is a graph-theoretic invariant that measures the minimum irreducible bidirectional information flow in a directed graph. It is the routing primitive that determines whether a query region of a knowledge graph requires single-pass retrieval (κ = 0) or iterative deliberation (κ > 0)."}]},{"id":"blk-70224","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-102989","text":"This spec defines:"}]},{"id":"blk-70225","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-70227","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-102990","text":"How κ is computed"}]}],"id":"blk-70226","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-70229","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-102991","text":"Where it is computed in the stack"}]}],"id":"blk-70228","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-70231","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-102992","text":"How it routes inference"}]}],"id":"blk-70230","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-70233","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-102993","text":"How it is surfaced to users"}]}],"id":"blk-70232","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-70235","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-102994","text":"How it integrates with each product"}]}],"id":"blk-70234","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-70236","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-102995","text":"2. Computation"}]},{"id":"blk-70237","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-102996","text":"2.1 Algorithm"}]},{"id":"blk-70238","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"function compute_kappa(graph):\n    # Pre-step: define node universe U from the analyzed subgraph/query result.\n    # Ignore any edge where src ∉ U or dst ∉ U.\n    # Exclude self-loops (u -> u) from adjacency for κ computation.\n    # Step 1: Find all strongly connected components\n    sccs = tarjan_scc(graph)                    # O(V + E)\n\n    # Step 2: For each nontrivial SCC (size > 1)\n    results = []\n    for scc in sccs where |scc| > 1:\n        # Step 3: Enumerate bipartitions, find minimum bidirectional cut\n        k = infinity\n        for (A, B) in nontrivial_bipartitions(scc):\n            edges_a_to_b = count_edges(A, B, graph)\n            edges_b_to_a = count_edges(B, A, graph)\n            bidirectional_cut = min(edges_a_to_b, edges_b_to_a)\n            k = min(k, bidirectional_cut)\n            if k == 0: break  # early exit (can't go lower)\n\n        # Step 4: Record SCC with its κ value and minimum-cut partition\n        results.append({\n            scc: scc,\n            kappa: k,\n            min_cut_partition: (A_min, B_min),\n            min_cut_edges: edges_achieving_minimum\n        })\n\n    return results"},{"id":"blk-70239","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-102997","text":"2.2 Complexity"}]},{"id":"blk-70240","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-70242","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-102998","marks":["bold"],"text":"SCC decomposition:"},{"id":"spn-102999","text":" O(V + E) via Tarjan's algorithm"}]}],"id":"blk-70241","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-70244","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-103000","marks":["bold"],"text":"κ computation per SCC:"},{"id":"spn-103001","text":" O(2^|SCC| × |SCC|²) in the worst case (enumerating all bipartitions)"}]}],"id":"blk-70243","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-70246","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-103002","marks":["bold"],"text":"Practical constraint:"},{"id":"spn-103003","text":" For SCCs up to ~20 nodes, bipartition enumeration is feasible in real time. For larger SCCs, use approximation:"}]}],"id":"blk-70245","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-70248","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-103004","text":"Return SCC size as a proxy for κ, with "},{"id":"spn-103005","marks":["code"],"text":"approximate: true"},{"id":"spn-103006","text":" flag"}]}],"id":"blk-70247","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-70250","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-103007","text":"κ field remains an integer (the estimate), never a symbol/atom/string"}]}],"id":"blk-70249","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-70252","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-103008","marks":["bold"],"text":"Node-universe rule (NORMATIVE):"},{"id":"spn-103009","text":" Analyze only the node set supplied by retrieval/query scope (or explicit "},{"id":"spn-103010","marks":["code"],"text":"node_ids"},{"id":"spn-103011","text":" input). Do not pull in external nodes implicitly during κ analysis."}]}],"id":"blk-70251","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-70254","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-103012","marks":["bold"],"text":"Self-loop rule (NORMATIVE):"},{"id":"spn-103013","text":" Exclude self-loops ("},{"id":"spn-103014","marks":["code"],"text":"source == target"},{"id":"spn-103015","text":") from κ adjacency and cut counts."}]}],"id":"blk-70253","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-70255","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-103016","text":"2.3 Incremental Updates"}]},{"id":"blk-70256","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-103017","text":"When an edge is added or removed from the knowledge graph:"}]},{"id":"blk-70257","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-70259","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-103018","marks":["bold"],"text":"Edge addition:"},{"id":"spn-103019","text":" Can only merge SCCs or enlarge existing ones. Re-run Tarjan on the affected component. If a new nontrivial SCC is formed, compute κ for it."}]}],"id":"blk-70258","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-70261","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-103020","marks":["bold"],"text":"Edge removal:"},{"id":"spn-103021","text":" Can only split SCCs or shrink them. Re-run Tarjan on the affected component. Recompute κ for any remaining nontrivial SCCs."}]}],"id":"blk-70260","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-70263","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-103022","marks":["bold"],"text":"Optimization:"},{"id":"spn-103023","text":" Maintain an SCC index alongside the knowledge graph. Incremental SCC algorithms (e.g., Bender, Fineman & Gilbert 2015) can update SCCs in O(V) amortized per edge change."}]}],"id":"blk-70262","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true},{"id":"blk-70264","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-103024","text":"2.4 Canonical Schema (NORMATIVE — all implementations must match)"}]},{"id":"blk-70265","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-103025","text":"Every κ topology result — whether from Elixir, JavaScript, or MCP JSON — uses these exact field names:"}]},{"id":"blk-70266","kind":"code","language":"json","text":"{\n  \"sccs\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"scc-0\",\n      \"nodes\": [\"node-a\", \"node-b\"],\n      \"kappa\": 2,\n      \"approximate\": false,\n      \"fault_line_edges\": [\n        {\"source\": \"node-a\", \"target\": \"node-b\"}\n      ],\n      \"routing\": \"deliberate\",\n      \"deliberation_budget\": {\n        \"max_iterations\": 3,\n        \"agent_count\": 2,\n        \"timeout_multiplier\": 2.0,\n        \"confidence_threshold\": 0.80\n      }\n    }\n  ],\n  \"dag_nodes\": [\"node-x\", \"node-y\"],\n  \"routing\": \"deliberate\",\n  \"max_kappa\": 2,\n  \"scc_count\": 1\n}"},{"id":"blk-70267","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-103026","marks":["bold"],"text":"Field name rules (resolves all drift):"}]},{"id":"blk-70268","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-70270","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-103027","text":"Top-level routing key: "},{"id":"spn-103028","marks":["code"],"text":"routing"},{"id":"spn-103029","text":" (not "},{"id":"spn-103030","marks":["code"],"text":"overall_routing"},{"id":"spn-103031","text":")"}]}],"id":"blk-70269","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-70272","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-103032","text":"Edge endpoints: "},{"id":"spn-103033","marks":["code"],"text":"source"},{"id":"spn-103034","text":" / "},{"id":"spn-103035","marks":["code"],"text":"target"},{"id":"spn-103036","text":" (not "},{"id":"spn-103037","marks":["code"],"text":"from"},{"id":"spn-103038","text":"/"},{"id":"spn-103039","marks":["code"],"text":"to"},{"id":"spn-103040","text":", not "},{"id":"spn-103041","marks":["code"],"text":"a"},{"id":"spn-103042","text":"/"},{"id":"spn-103043","marks":["code"],"text":"b"},{"id":"spn-103044","text":")"}]}],"id":"blk-70271","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-70274","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-103045","text":"Fault lines: "},{"id":"spn-103046","marks":["code"],"text":"fault_line_edges"},{"id":"spn-103047","text":" (not "},{"id":"spn-103048","marks":["code"],"text":"min_cut_edges"},{"id":"spn-103049","text":")"}]}],"id":"blk-70273","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-70276","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-103050","text":"κ type: always "},{"id":"spn-103051","marks":["code"],"text":"integer"},{"id":"spn-103052","text":" (never string, atom, or symbol)"}]}],"id":"blk-70275","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-70278","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-103053","text":"Approximation: "},{"id":"spn-103054","marks":["code"],"text":"\"approximate\": true"},{"id":"spn-103055","text":" boolean flag on the SCC object; "},{"id":"spn-103056","marks":["code"],"text":"kappa"},{"id":"spn-103057","text":" still holds the integer estimate"}]}],"id":"blk-70277","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-70280","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-103058","text":"Routing values: "},{"id":"spn-103059","marks":["code"],"text":"\"fast\""},{"id":"spn-103060","text":" or "},{"id":"spn-103061","marks":["code"],"text":"\"deliberate\""},{"id":"spn-103062","text":" (strings in JSON, atoms "},{"id":"spn-103063","marks":["code"],"text":":fast"},{"id":"spn-103064","text":"/"},{"id":"spn-103065","marks":["code"],"text":":deliberate"},{"id":"spn-103066","text":" in Elixir, strings in JS)"}]}],"id":"blk-70279","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-70281","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-103067","marks":["bold"],"text":"Schema boundary rules (NORMATIVE):"}]},{"id":"blk-70282","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-70284","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-103068","marks":["bold"],"text":"On MCP/JSON boundaries:"},{"id":"spn-103069","text":" use canonical snake_case keys exactly as defined in §2.4 ("},{"id":"spn-103070","marks":["code"],"text":"fault_line_edges"},{"id":"spn-103071","text":", "},{"id":"spn-103072","marks":["code"],"text":"max_kappa"},{"id":"spn-103073","text":", "},{"id":"spn-103074","marks":["code"],"text":"scc_count"},{"id":"spn-103075","text":", etc.)."}]}],"id":"blk-70283","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-70286","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-103076","marks":["bold"],"text":"Inside Elixir runtime:"},{"id":"spn-103077","text":" atoms are allowed for routing values ("},{"id":"spn-103078","marks":["code"],"text":":fast"},{"id":"spn-103079","text":", "},{"id":"spn-103080","marks":["code"],"text":":deliberate"},{"id":"spn-103081","text":"), but keys remain canonical and are serialized to JSON strings at the boundary."}]}],"id":"blk-70285","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-70288","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-103082","marks":["bold"],"text":"Inside JavaScript UI code:"},{"id":"spn-103083","text":" camelCase mirrors are allowed for local-only objects ("},{"id":"spn-103084","marks":["code"],"text":"faultLineEdges"},{"id":"spn-103085","text":", "},{"id":"spn-103086","marks":["code"],"text":"maxKappa"},{"id":"spn-103087","text":", "},{"id":"spn-103088","marks":["code"],"text":"sccCount"},{"id":"spn-103089","text":") for ergonomics, but any network payload or persisted topology record must be converted back to canonical snake_case."}]}],"id":"blk-70287","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-70289","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-103090","marks":["bold"],"text":"Elixir atom mapping:"}]},{"id":"blk-70290","kind":"code","language":"elixir","text":"# Elixir uses atoms internally, converts to strings for MCP JSON\n:fast       → \"fast\"\n:deliberate → \"deliberate\""},{"id":"blk-70291","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-103091","marks":["bold"],"text":"JavaScript mapping (local only):"}]},{"id":"blk-70292","kind":"code","language":"javascript","text":"// Local object ergonomics\n{ faultLineEdges, maxKappa, sccCount, routing }\n\n// MCP / wire payloads must remain canonical snake_case\n{ fault_line_edges, max_kappa, scc_count, routing }"},{"id":"blk-70293","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-103092","text":"3. Routing Logic"}]},{"id":"blk-70294","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-103093","text":"3.1 The κ Router"}]},{"id":"blk-70295","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-103094","text":"The κ router sits between memory retrieval and reasoning. It inspects the topological structure of the retrieved subgraph and makes a routing decision."}]},{"id":"blk-70296","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"function kappa_route(retrieved_subgraph):\n    scc_analysis = compute_kappa(retrieved_subgraph)\n\n    dag_context = nodes NOT in any nontrivial SCC\n    scc_contexts = scc_analysis  # list of {scc, kappa, fault_line_edges, ...}\n\n    # DAG regions: single-pass retrieval\n    retrieval_context = topological_sort_and_collect(dag_context)\n\n    # SCC regions: flag for deliberation\n    deliberation_tasks = []\n    for scc_info in scc_contexts:\n        deliberation_tasks.append({\n            nodes: scc_info.scc,\n            kappa: scc_info.kappa,\n            fault_lines: scc_info.fault_line_edges,\n            budget: deliberation_budget(scc_info.kappa)\n        })\n\n    return {\n        retrieval_context: retrieval_context,\n        deliberation_tasks: deliberation_tasks,\n        routing: \"fast\" if len(deliberation_tasks) == 0 else \"deliberate\"\n    }"},{"id":"blk-70297","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-103095","text":"3.2 Deliberation Budget Function"}]},{"id":"blk-70298","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-103096","text":"The deliberation budget maps κ to concrete inference parameters. This is an engineering heuristic (not proved — to be tuned empirically). Caps on "},{"id":"spn-103097","marks":["code"],"text":"max_iterations"},{"id":"spn-103098","text":" and "},{"id":"spn-103099","marks":["code"],"text":"confidence_threshold"},{"id":"spn-103100","text":" are required to prevent runaway values when "},{"id":"spn-103101","marks":["code"],"text":"approximate: true"},{"id":"spn-103102","text":" SCCs use size-based κ estimates:"}]},{"id":"blk-70299","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"function deliberation_budget(kappa):\n    return {\n        max_iterations: min(kappa + 1, 4),\n        agent_count: min(kappa, 3),\n        timeout_multiplier: min(1.0 + 0.5*kappa, 3.5),\n        confidence_threshold: min(0.7 + 0.05*kappa, 0.95)\n    }"},{"id":"blk-70300","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-103103","text":"3.3 The Fast Path vs. Deliberation Path"}]},{"id":"blk-70301","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"             ┌─────────────────┐\n             │  Query arrives   │\n             └────────┬────────┘\n                      │\n                      ▼\n             ┌─────────────────┐\n             │  &memory.recall  │   Graphonomous retrieves relevant subgraph\n             └────────┬────────┘\n                      │\n                      ▼\n             ┌─────────────────┐\n             │  κ Router        │   Compute SCCs, κ values\n             └────────┬────────┘\n                      │\n              ┌───────┴────────┐\n              │                │\n         κ = 0 (all DAG)    κ > 0 (has SCCs)\n              │                │\n              ▼                ▼\n       ┌──────────┐    ┌──────────────┐\n       │ Fast Path │    │  Deliberation │\n       │ single    │    │  &reason via  │\n       │ pass      │    │  Deliberatic  │\n       │ retrieval │    │  κ-informed   │\n       └─────┬────┘    │  budget       │\n             │         └──────┬───────┘\n             │                │\n             └───────┬────────┘\n                     │\n                     ▼\n             ┌──────────────┐\n             │  &memory.learn │   Results feed back into graph\n             └──────────────┘"},{"id":"blk-70302","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-103104","text":"4. Product Integration"}]},{"id":"blk-70303","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-103105","text":"4.1 Graphonomous"}]},{"id":"blk-70304","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-103106","marks":["bold"],"text":"Where κ lives:"},{"id":"spn-103107","text":" Computed at query time on the retrieved subgraph. Cached per SCC in the knowledge graph index; invalidated on edge changes."}]},{"id":"blk-70305","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-103108","marks":["bold"],"text":"What changes:"}]},{"id":"blk-70306","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-70308","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-103109","marks":["code"],"text":"Retriever.retrieve/2"},{"id":"spn-103110","text":" now returns a "},{"id":"spn-103111","marks":["code"],"text":"topology"},{"id":"spn-103112","text":" key alongside existing "},{"id":"spn-103113","marks":["code"],"text":"results"},{"id":"spn-103114","text":", "},{"id":"spn-103115","marks":["code"],"text":"causal_context"},{"id":"spn-103116","text":", "},{"id":"spn-103117","marks":["code"],"text":"stats"}]}],"id":"blk-70307","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-70310","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-103118","text":"New module "},{"id":"spn-103119","marks":["code"],"text":"Graphonomous.Topology"},{"id":"spn-103120","text":" computes and returns the full SCC analysis for a given subgraph"}]}],"id":"blk-70309","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-70312","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-103121","text":"New function "},{"id":"spn-103122","marks":["code"],"text":"Store.list_edges_between/1"},{"id":"spn-103123","text":" fetches edges within a node set"}]}],"id":"blk-70311","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-70313","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-103124","marks":["bold"],"text":"MCP tool: `analyze_topology` (NEW standalone tool):"}]},{"id":"blk-70314","kind":"code","language":"json","text":"{\n  \"name\": \"analyze_topology\",\n  \"description\": \"Compute topological structure (SCCs, κ values, routing decision) for a set of nodes in the knowledge graph.\",\n  \"inputSchema\": {\n    \"type\": \"object\",\n    \"properties\": {\n      \"node_ids\": {\n        \"type\": \"array\",\n        \"items\": { \"type\": \"string\" },\n        \"description\": \"Node IDs to analyze. If omitted, analyzes the full graph.\"\n      },\n      \"query\": {\n        \"type\": \"string\",\n        \"description\": \"Optional query text. If provided, retrieves relevant nodes first, then analyzes their topology.\"\n      }\n    }\n  }\n}"},{"id":"blk-70315","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-103125","marks":["bold"],"text":"MCP tool: `retrieve_context` (EXISTING — augmented with topology):"}]},{"id":"blk-70316","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-103126","text":"The existing "},{"id":"spn-103127","marks":["code"],"text":"retrieve_context"},{"id":"spn-103128","text":" tool gains a "},{"id":"spn-103129","marks":["code"],"text":"topology"},{"id":"spn-103130","text":" field in its response. No new tool name — same endpoint, richer response:"}]},{"id":"blk-70317","kind":"code","language":"json","text":"{\n  \"status\": \"ok\",\n  \"query\": \"company strategy\",\n  \"count\": 7,\n  \"results\": [\"...existing results...\"],\n  \"causal_context\": [\"...existing...\"],\n  \"stats\": {\"...existing...\"},\n  \"topology\": {\n    \"sccs\": [\n      {\n        \"id\": \"scc-0\",\n        \"nodes\": [\"market-share\", \"revenue\", \"r-and-d\", \"product-quality\", \"customer-retention\"],\n        \"kappa\": 1,\n        \"approximate\": false,\n        \"fault_line_edges\": [\n          {\"source\": \"product-quality\", \"target\": \"market-share\"}\n        ],\n        \"routing\": \"deliberate\",\n        \"deliberation_budget\": {\n          \"max_iterations\": 2,\n          \"agent_count\": 1,\n          \"timeout_multiplier\": 1.5,\n          \"confidence_threshold\": 0.75\n        }\n      }\n    ],\n    \"dag_nodes\": [\"founding-date\", \"ceo-name\", \"headquarters\"],\n    \"routing\": \"deliberate\",\n    \"max_kappa\": 1,\n    \"scc_count\": 1\n  }\n}"},{"id":"blk-70318","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-103131","text":"4.2 Deliberatic"}]},{"id":"blk-70319","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-103132","marks":["bold"],"text":"What changes:"}]},{"id":"blk-70320","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-70322","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-103133","text":"Accepts "},{"id":"spn-103134","marks":["code"],"text":"kappa"},{"id":"spn-103135","text":" and "},{"id":"spn-103136","marks":["code"],"text":"fault_line_edges"},{"id":"spn-103137","text":" as input parameters on its deliberation endpoint."}]}],"id":"blk-70321","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-70324","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-103138","text":"Uses "},{"id":"spn-103139","marks":["code"],"text":"kappa"},{"id":"spn-103140","text":" to set argumentation depth (number of rounds)."}]}],"id":"blk-70323","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-70326","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-103141","text":"Uses "},{"id":"spn-103142","marks":["code"],"text":"fault_line_edges"},{"id":"spn-103143","text":" (minimum-cut edges) to generate the initial propositions that agents must argue about — these are the critical bidirectional dependencies."}]}],"id":"blk-70325","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-70327","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-103144","marks":["bold"],"text":"MCP tool additions:"}]},{"id":"blk-70328","kind":"code","language":"json","text":"{\n  \"name\": \"deliberate_on_scc\",\n  \"description\": \"Run structured argumentation on a strongly connected knowledge cluster. Uses κ to set deliberation budget and fault lines to seed propositions.\",\n  \"inputSchema\": {\n    \"type\": \"object\",\n    \"properties\": {\n      \"scc_nodes\": { \"type\": \"array\", \"items\": { \"type\": \"string\" } },\n      \"scc_edges\": { \"type\": \"array\" },\n      \"kappa\": { \"type\": \"integer\" },\n      \"fault_line_edges\": { \"type\": \"array\" },\n      \"governance\": { \"type\": \"object\" }\n    }\n  }\n}"},{"id":"blk-70329","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-103145","marks":["bold"],"text":"Key insight:"},{"id":"spn-103146","text":" Deliberatic doesn't need to know about graph theory. It receives a set of propositions (derived from fault lines), a budget (derived from κ), and it argues. The graph intelligence lives in Graphonomous; the argumentation intelligence lives in Deliberatic. κ is the handshake between them."}]},{"id":"blk-70330","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-103147","text":"4.3 BendScript"}]},{"id":"blk-70331","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-103148","marks":["bold"],"text":"What changes:"}]},{"id":"blk-70332","kind":"heading","level":4,"spans":[{"id":"spn-103149","text":"Directed-Edge Policy (NORMATIVE)"}]},{"id":"blk-70333","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-103150","text":"BendScript edges have a "},{"id":"spn-103151","marks":["code"],"text":"kind"},{"id":"spn-103152","text":" property. For κ computation, edge directionality is determined by kind:"}]},{"head":[{"id":"blk-70335","spans":[{"id":"spn-103153","text":"Edge kind"}]},{"id":"blk-70336","spans":[{"id":"spn-103154","text":"Directionality for κ"}]},{"id":"blk-70337","spans":[{"id":"spn-103155","text":"Rationale"}]}],"id":"blk-70334","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-70338","spans":[{"id":"spn-103156","marks":["code"],"text":"causal"}]},{"id":"blk-70339","spans":[{"id":"spn-103157","marks":["bold"],"text":"Directed"},{"id":"spn-103158","text":" (a → b)"}]},{"id":"blk-70340","spans":[{"id":"spn-103159","text":"Cause precedes effect"}]}],[{"id":"blk-70341","spans":[{"id":"spn-103160","marks":["code"],"text":"temporal"}]},{"id":"blk-70342","spans":[{"id":"spn-103161","marks":["bold"],"text":"Directed"},{"id":"spn-103162","text":" (a → b)"}]},{"id":"blk-70343","spans":[{"id":"spn-103163","text":"Before precedes after"}]}],[{"id":"blk-70344","spans":[{"id":"spn-103164","marks":["code"],"text":"context"}]},{"id":"blk-70345","spans":[{"id":"spn-103165","marks":["bold"],"text":"Skip"},{"id":"spn-103166","text":" (excluded from κ graph)"}]},{"id":"blk-70346","spans":[{"id":"spn-103167","text":"Symmetric, no feedback"}]}],[{"id":"blk-70347","spans":[{"id":"spn-103168","marks":["code"],"text":"associative"}]},{"id":"blk-70348","spans":[{"id":"spn-103169","marks":["bold"],"text":"Skip"},{"id":"spn-103170","text":" (excluded from κ graph)"}]},{"id":"blk-70349","spans":[{"id":"spn-103171","text":"Symmetric, no feedback"}]}],[{"id":"blk-70350","spans":[{"id":"spn-103172","marks":["code"],"text":"user"}]},{"id":"blk-70351","spans":[{"id":"spn-103173","marks":["bold"],"text":"Skip"},{"id":"spn-103174","text":" (excluded from κ graph)"}]},{"id":"blk-70352","spans":[{"id":"spn-103175","text":"Ambiguous directionality"}]}]]},{"id":"blk-70353","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-103176","text":"This is a "},{"id":"spn-103177","marks":["bold"],"text":"hard rule"},{"id":"spn-103178","text":", not a toggle. Only "},{"id":"spn-103179","marks":["code"],"text":"causal"},{"id":"spn-103180","text":" and "},{"id":"spn-103181","marks":["code"],"text":"temporal"},{"id":"spn-103182","text":" edges participate in SCC/κ computation. The filter constant:"}]},{"id":"blk-70354","kind":"code","language":"javascript","text":"const DIRECTED_KINDS = ['causal', 'temporal'];"},{"id":"blk-70355","kind":"heading","level":4,"spans":[{"id":"spn-103183","text":"Visual Layer"}]},{"id":"blk-70356","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-70358","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-103184","marks":["bold"],"text":"SCC clusters rendered visually:"},{"id":"spn-103185","text":" Nodes within a nontrivial SCC share a colored halo or background region. Color intensity scales with κ."}]}],"id":"blk-70357","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-70360","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-103186","marks":["bold"],"text":"Minimum-cut edges highlighted:"},{"id":"spn-103187","text":" Fault-line edges rendered in dashed style ("},{"id":"spn-103188","marks":["code"],"text":"ctx.setLineDash([6, 4])"},{"id":"spn-103189","text":") with brighter color."}]}],"id":"blk-70359","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-70362","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-103190","marks":["bold"],"text":"κ badge on SCC clusters:"},{"id":"spn-103191","text":" Each SCC cluster shows its κ value as a small badge, e.g., \"κ=2\"."}]}],"id":"blk-70361","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-70363","kind":"heading","level":4,"spans":[{"id":"spn-103192","text":"Interaction Layer"}]},{"id":"blk-70364","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-70366","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-103193","marks":["bold"],"text":"Topology preview via context menu:"},{"id":"spn-103194","text":" When the user right-clicks a node and selects \"Connect to…\" (a new context menu item), BendScript shows candidate target nodes with topology impact annotations:"}]}],"id":"blk-70365","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-70368","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-103195","text":"\"→ NodeX: creates feedback loop (κ: 0→1)\""}]}],"id":"blk-70367","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-70370","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-103196","text":"\"→ NodeY: strengthens loop (κ: 1→2)\""}]}],"id":"blk-70369","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-70372","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-103197","text":"\"→ NodeZ: no topological change\""}]}],"id":"blk-70371","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-70374","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-103198","marks":["bold"],"text":"\"Bend\" action:"},{"id":"spn-103199","text":" Right-click context menu on DAG nodes — automatically suggests the nearest edge that would create a feedback loop."}]}],"id":"blk-70373","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-70376","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-103200","marks":["bold"],"text":"\"Unbend\" action:"},{"id":"spn-103201","text":" Right-click context menu on SCC nodes — identifies the fault-line edge and offers to remove it."}]}],"id":"blk-70375","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-70377","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-103202","marks":["bold"],"text":"Note:"},{"id":"spn-103203","text":" BendScript does NOT currently have drag-to-connect edge creation. The topology preview is accessed via the context menu \"Connect to…\" flow. Do not implement drag-to-connect in this phase."}]},{"id":"blk-70378","kind":"heading","level":4,"spans":[{"id":"spn-103204","text":"HUD"}]},{"id":"blk-70379","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-70381","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-103205","marks":["bold"],"text":"Global κ display:"},{"id":"spn-103206","text":" The existing HUD gains a κ readout showing the maximum κ across all SCCs in the graph, and a count of SCCs."}]}],"id":"blk-70380","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-70383","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-103207","marks":["bold"],"text":"Routing indicator:"},{"id":"spn-103208","text":" \"mode: RETRIEVAL\" (all κ = 0) or \"mode: DELIBERATION\" (any κ > 0)."}]}],"id":"blk-70382","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-70384","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-103209","text":"4.4 The [&] Protocol"}]},{"id":"blk-70385","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-103210","marks":["bold"],"text":"Grammar extension:"}]},{"id":"blk-70386","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"# Extended [&] capability grammar — topology-aware routing\nTopologyOp      := \"&topology\" \".\" (\"analyze\" | \"route\" | \"kappa\")\n\n# Updated pipeline pattern\nInferencePipeline :=\n    \"&memory.recall\" \"(\" QueryExpr \")\"\n    \"|>\" \"&topology.analyze\" \"()\"\n    \"|>\" \"&topology.route\" \"()\"\n    \"|>\" \"&reason.deliberate\" \"(\" \"budget:\" \":κ\" \")\"\n    \"|>\" \"&memory.learn\" \"()\""},{"id":"blk-70387","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-103211","marks":["bold"],"text":"Schema extension (ampersand.schema.json):"}]},{"id":"blk-70388","kind":"code","language":"json","text":"{\n  \"capabilities\": {\n    \"&topology.analyze\": {\n      \"provider\": \"graphonomous\",\n      \"description\": \"Compute SCC decomposition and κ values for a subgraph\",\n      \"config\": {\n        \"max_scc_size_for_exact\": 20,\n        \"approximation_strategy\": \"scc_size_proxy\"\n      }\n    },\n    \"&topology.route\": {\n      \"provider\": \"builtin\",\n      \"description\": \"Route inference based on κ: DAG regions → fast path, SCC regions → deliberation\",\n      \"config\": {\n        \"deliberation_provider\": \"deliberatic\",\n        \"fast_path_provider\": \"graphonomous\"\n      }\n    }\n  }\n}"},{"id":"blk-70389","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-103212","text":"4.5 TickTickClock"}]},{"id":"blk-70390","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-103213","marks":["bold"],"text":"Connection:"},{"id":"spn-103214","text":" For discrete time-series dynamics, the transition graph of the system has κ > 0 if and only if the system has a periodic orbit. TickTickClock can use this as a formal periodicity detector:"}]},{"id":"blk-70391","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-70393","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-103215","text":"Discretize time-series data into state transitions"}]}],"id":"blk-70392","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-70395","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-103216","text":"Build the transition graph"}]}],"id":"blk-70394","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-70397","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-103217","text":"Compute κ"}]}],"id":"blk-70396","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-70399","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-103218","text":"κ > 0 → periodic pattern detected, flag for temporal reasoning"}]}],"id":"blk-70398","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-70401","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-103219","text":"κ = 0 → pure drift, no recurrence"}]}],"id":"blk-70400","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-70402","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-103220","text":"This is a secondary integration (TickTickClock already has Mamba SSM for pattern detection), but it provides a complementary structural signal."}]},{"id":"blk-70403","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-103221","text":"4.6 OpenSentience"}]},{"id":"blk-70404","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-103222","marks":["bold"],"text":"Role:"},{"id":"spn-103223","text":" Research home for the theoretical foundations. Hosts:"}]},{"id":"blk-70405","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-70407","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-103224","text":"The κ paper (theoretical background, proofs, categorical framework)"}]}],"id":"blk-70406","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-70409","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-103225","text":"The proof code (runnable verification)"}]}],"id":"blk-70408","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-70411","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-103226","text":"Interactive demos (live κ computation on user-constructed graphs)"}]}],"id":"blk-70410","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-70413","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-103227","text":"The original Scale Topology Axis essay (broader theoretical context connecting κ to physics, cosmology, and consciousness science)"}]}],"id":"blk-70412","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-70414","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-103228","text":"5. Implementation Priority"}]},{"id":"blk-70415","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-103229","text":"Phase 1: Core (ship first)"}]},{"id":"blk-70416","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-70418","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-103230","text":"[ ] Port κ computation to Elixir (Graphonomous server-side)"}]}],"id":"blk-70417","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-70420","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-103231","text":"[ ] Port κ computation to JavaScript (BendScript client-side)"}]}],"id":"blk-70419","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-70422","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-103232","text":"[ ] Integrate Tarjan's SCC into Graphonomous's graph index"}]}],"id":"blk-70421","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-70424","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-103233","text":"[ ] Return topology annotations from "},{"id":"spn-103234","marks":["code"],"text":"retrieve_context"}]}],"id":"blk-70423","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-70426","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-103235","text":"[ ] Add SCC visualization to BendScript canvas"}]}],"id":"blk-70425","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-70427","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-103236","text":"Phase 2: Routing (ship second)"}]},{"id":"blk-70428","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-70430","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-103237","text":"[ ] Implement κ router in the [&] pipeline"}]}],"id":"blk-70429","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-70432","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-103238","text":"[ ] Connect κ router to Deliberatic trigger"}]}],"id":"blk-70431","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-70434","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-103239","text":"[ ] Add deliberation budget function"}]}],"id":"blk-70433","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-70436","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-103240","text":"[ ] Test on real knowledge graph queries: does κ-aware routing improve answer quality?"}]}],"id":"blk-70435","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-70437","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-103241","text":"Phase 3: Polish (ship third)"}]},{"id":"blk-70438","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-70440","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-103242","text":"[ ] BendScript topology preview via context menu"}]}],"id":"blk-70439","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-70442","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-103243","text":"[ ] Bend/Unbend context menu actions"}]}],"id":"blk-70441","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-70444","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-103244","text":"[ ] HUD κ display and routing indicator"}]}],"id":"blk-70443","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-70446","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-103245","text":"[ ] TickTickClock periodicity detection via κ"}]}],"id":"blk-70445","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-70448","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-103246","text":"[ ] OpenSentience publication of κ paper and demos"}]}],"id":"blk-70447","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-70449","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-103247","text":"Phase 4: Optimization"}]},{"id":"blk-70450","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-70452","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-103248","text":"[ ] Incremental SCC maintenance (avoid full recomputation on every edge change)"}]}],"id":"blk-70451","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-70454","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-103249","text":"[ ] Approximate κ for large SCCs (> 20 nodes)"}]}],"id":"blk-70453","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-70456","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-103250","text":"[ ] Benchmark: latency impact of topology computation on query path"}]}],"id":"blk-70455","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-70458","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-103251","text":"[ ] A/B test: κ-routed inference vs. uniform retrieval on quality metrics"}]}],"id":"blk-70457","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-70459","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-103252","text":"6. Success Metrics"}]},{"head":[{"id":"blk-70461","spans":[{"id":"spn-103253","text":"Metric"}]},{"id":"blk-70462","spans":[{"id":"spn-103254","text":"Baseline (no κ)"}]},{"id":"blk-70463","spans":[{"id":"spn-103255","text":"Target (with κ)"}]},{"id":"blk-70464","spans":[{"id":"spn-103256","text":"How to Measure"}]}],"id":"blk-70460","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-70465","spans":[{"id":"spn-103257","text":"Answer coherence on circular topics"}]},{"id":"blk-70466","spans":[{"id":"spn-103258","text":"Human eval ~60%"}]},{"id":"blk-70467","spans":[{"id":"spn-103259","text":"Human eval ~80%"}]},{"id":"blk-70468","spans":[{"id":"spn-103260","text":"Blind eval on queries touching SCCs"}]}],[{"id":"blk-70469","spans":[{"id":"spn-103261","text":"Unnecessary deliberation calls"}]},{"id":"blk-70470","spans":[{"id":"spn-103262","text":"N/A (no routing)"}]},{"id":"blk-70471","spans":[{"id":"spn-103263","text":"< 20% of queries"}]},{"id":"blk-70472","spans":[{"id":"spn-103264","text":"Track κ=0 queries that hit deliberation anyway"}]}],[{"id":"blk-70473","spans":[{"id":"spn-103265","text":"Deliberation convergence speed"}]},{"id":"blk-70474","spans":[{"id":"spn-103266","text":"Fixed rounds"}]},{"id":"blk-70475","spans":[{"id":"spn-103267","text":"κ+1 rounds avg"}]},{"id":"blk-70476","spans":[{"id":"spn-103268","text":"Measure rounds to convergence"}]}],[{"id":"blk-70477","spans":[{"id":"spn-103269","text":"User engagement in BendScript"}]},{"id":"blk-70478","spans":[{"id":"spn-103270","text":"Nodes/edges per session"}]},{"id":"blk-70479","spans":[{"id":"spn-103271","text":"+30%"}]},{"id":"blk-70480","spans":[{"id":"spn-103272","text":"Track topology actions (bend/unbend/stargate)"}]}],[{"id":"blk-70481","spans":[{"id":"spn-103273","text":"OpenSentience traffic"}]},{"id":"blk-70482","spans":[{"id":"spn-103274","text":"Baseline"}]},{"id":"blk-70483","spans":[{"id":"spn-103275","text":"Organic from dev community"}]},{"id":"blk-70484","spans":[{"id":"spn-103276","text":"Track referrals from product UIs"}]}]]},{"id":"blk-70485","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-103277","text":"7. Instrumentation Requirements (NEW in v0.2.0)"}]},{"id":"blk-70486","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-103278","text":"All κ computation must emit telemetry. This is required for Gate C (performance) and Gate D (product effect) validation."}]},{"id":"blk-70487","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-103279","text":"7.1 Latency Counters (Elixir — "},{"id":"spn-103280","marks":["code"],"text":":telemetry"},{"id":"spn-103281","text":")"}]},{"id":"blk-70488","kind":"code","language":"elixir","text":"# Emit on every topology computation\n# REQUIRED UNIT: duration_ms (float milliseconds)\n# If measured via :timer.tc/1, convert with: duration_ms = duration_us / 1000.0\n:telemetry.execute(\n  [:graphonomous, :topology, :analyze],\n  %{duration_ms: elapsed_ms, node_count: n, edge_count: e},\n  %{scc_count: scc_count, max_kappa: max_kappa, routing: routing}\n)"},{"id":"blk-70489","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-103282","text":"Track:"}]},{"id":"blk-70490","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-70492","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-103283","marks":["code"],"text":"topology.analyze.duration_ms"},{"id":"spn-103284","text":" — p50, p95, p99 (canonical latency metric)"}]}],"id":"blk-70491","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-70494","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-103285","marks":["code"],"text":"topology.analyze.node_count"},{"id":"spn-103286","text":" — distribution of subgraph sizes"}]}],"id":"blk-70493","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-70496","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-103287","marks":["code"],"text":"topology.analyze.edge_count"},{"id":"spn-103288","text":" — distribution of subgraph densities"}]}],"id":"blk-70495","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-70498","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-103289","marks":["code"],"text":"topology.analyze.scc_count"},{"id":"spn-103290","text":" — how often SCCs are found"}]}],"id":"blk-70497","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-70500","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-103291","marks":["code"],"text":"topology.analyze.routing.deliberate_ratio"},{"id":"spn-103292","text":" — deliberate / total analyzes"}]}],"id":"blk-70499","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-70502","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-103293","marks":["code"],"text":"topology.analyze.self_loop_filtered_count"},{"id":"spn-103294","text":" — number of self-loops ignored during adjacency construction"}]}],"id":"blk-70501","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-70503","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-103295","text":"7.2 Routing Decision Counters"}]},{"id":"blk-70504","kind":"code","language":"elixir","text":":telemetry.execute(\n  [:graphonomous, :topology, :route],\n  %{},\n  %{decision: :fast | :deliberate, max_kappa: max_kappa, trigger: :retrieve_context | :analyze_topology}\n)"},{"id":"blk-70505","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-103296","text":"Track:"}]},{"id":"blk-70506","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-70508","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-103297","marks":["code"],"text":"topology.route.fast_count"},{"id":"spn-103298","text":" — queries routed to fast path"}]}],"id":"blk-70507","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-70510","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-103299","marks":["code"],"text":"topology.route.deliberate_count"},{"id":"spn-103300","text":" — queries routed to deliberation"}]}],"id":"blk-70509","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-70512","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-103301","marks":["code"],"text":"topology.route.deliberate_ratio"},{"id":"spn-103302","text":" — deliberate / total (target: < 30% on typical workloads)"}]}],"id":"blk-70511","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-70513","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-103303","text":"7.3 BendScript Performance (JavaScript — "},{"id":"spn-103304","marks":["code"],"text":"performance.now()"},{"id":"spn-103305","text":")"}]},{"id":"blk-70514","kind":"code","language":"javascript","text":"const t0 = performance.now();\nconst topo = analyzeTopology(plane);\nconst elapsed = performance.now() - t0;\nconsole.debug(`[κ] topology: ${elapsed.toFixed(1)}ms, maxκ=${topo.maxKappa}, sccs=${topo.sccCount}`);"},{"id":"blk-70515","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-103306","text":"Target: < 50ms at 100 nodes."}]},{"id":"blk-70516","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-103307","marks":["italic"],"text":"Spec version: 0.2.0. Status: Draft (normalized). Depends on: kappa_reference.py (computation), kappa_theory_applied.md (theoretical foundations). Products affected: Graphonomous, Deliberatic, BendScript, [&] Protocol, TickTickClock, OpenSentience."}]}],"edges":[],"id":"bagaaieraqdqsztddkeanodiharbraygahm2augqi3a6niu5j2eayfuhqigza","vocabulary":"ampersand.docs.fs.v1"}